                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "The Casper Snug foam mattress is only available in twin and full size. Having the correct support ensures the comfort and longevity of our foam mattresses. Casper mattresses are designed to work on a firm, solid surface like our foundation. For slatted frames, we recommend using bed slats that are flat, wooden, and no more than 4 inches apart. With a height of 8 inches, the Snug is also compatible with most standard bunk bed frames. "
              }
            },{
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "When is the best time to transition from a toddler bed to a big kid bed?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "The best time to transition from a toddler bed varies by child but here are some signs to look out for:Approaching the size\/weight limit of current toddler bedDifficulty getting or staying comfortableSneaking into your bedroom at nighttimeKeeping safety and comfort in mind, this creates a great opportunity to update your kid\u0026#39;s bedtime routine. Help your child develop healthy sleep habits and get comfortable falling asleep in their room consistently. The Snug is the perfect big kid bed with a medium-firm feel that is just as soothing as it is supportive for all night comfort. At 8 inches, the lower profile makes getting in and out of bed easier for your child transitioning from the safety rails of their old crib or toddler bed. The Snug also comes with two 5-sided mattress protectors – we understand that accidents happen and want to support everywhere we can. Read more about transitioning from a toddler bed to a big kid bed on our blog."
              }
            },{
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "How does Casper help support my child’s bedtime routine?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Casper designs products that encourage good sleep habits and routines. The Snug is a kids\u0026#39; mattress built with little ones in mind, but supportive enough for you to easily doze off during storytime together. Thanks to our high quality materials and thoughtful design, you can rely on this mattress to support your child through multiple stages of development."
              }
            },{
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Does Casper have a kids size mattress protector? ",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "The Snug comes with two 5-sided mattress protectors so you always have a clean one on hand.  Accidents happen! Made with breathable materials for extra comfort and a smooth polyester case, Casper’s soft-touch mattress protectors ensure a crinkle-free and comfortable experience. "
              }
            },{
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "What makes a kids mattress different from a crib mattress?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Crib mattresses and kids mattresses are designed for very different stages of development, and the differences go beyond just size.Crib mattresses are intentionally firm and thin (typically 4 to 6 inches) to reduce the risk of suffocation for infants and toddlers who don\u0026#39;t yet have full motor control. They\u0026#39;re built to fit the standardized dimensions of a crib (28\u0026quot; x 52\u0026quot;) and are regulated by strict federal safety standards for that reason.Kids mattresses, like The Casper Snug™, are designed for children who have outgrown their crib or toddler bed and are ready for more comfort and support as they grow.If your child is approaching the size or weight limit of their crib or toddler bed, it may be time to make the switch. "
              }
